# MCP Servers

The following MCP servers are available. Always prefer them over shell commands or CLI tools when applicable.

## Server Names (use exact names with `user-` prefix)

| Config Name     | Agent Server Name      | Use For                                      |
| --------------- | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Vercel          | `user-Vercel`          | Deployments, projects, logs, domains         |
| Supabase        | `user-Supabase`        | Database queries, migrations, edge functions |
| Chrome DevTools | `user-Chrome DevTools` | Browser inspection, performance profiling    |
| Context7        | `user-Context7`        | Up-to-date library/framework documentation   |
| _(built-in)_    | `cursor-ide-browser`   | Browser testing and web automation           |

## Usage Rules

- Use `user-Vercel` instead of running `vercel` CLI commands
- Use `user-Supabase` instead of running raw `psql` or `supabase` CLI commands
- Use `user-Context7` when you need current docs for any library before writing code
- Always read the tool schema from the mcps folder before calling a tool

## Tool Discovery

Before calling an unknown tool, list the available tools for that server from the mcps folder in the Cursor projects directory. Read the relevant JSON schema file before making any `call_mcp_tool` call.
